Subject: [PATCH 02374/11362] [outer-loop] tn36 L7: CORRECT diagnosis -- timed
 spike-traps, NOT transforms-during-maze (not solved, no fabrication)

Operator asked to 'extend the multi-run planner for transforms-during-maze and
solve L7' -- but investigating L7 showed the premise (my own prior speculative
note) was WRONG. L7 is pure-position (no transform); its real mechanic is TIMED
SPIKE-TRAPS:
 - ekdwmirldx = blinking spikes at y[16,20) x[37,61), invisible at start.
 - jmwdvdqntf toggles their visibility every 3 moves (oocupkguhu%3==2).
 - moving into / being caught on a VISIBLE spike DISABLES the object (qobvpoiega).
 - confirmed: straight 5-ups dies at (41,16) when the move-2 toggle turns the
   spikes on under the object.
The y[16,20) band is fully walled except x[37,61) when spikes are invisible; the
safe-crossing window collides with the lethal toggle, and no checkpoint sits where
a single run could time the crossing. Solving L7 needs a TIMED-STATE path-planner
(position x run-move-index x spike-parity) over the multi-run structure -- a real
new build, not a quick extension.

HONEST: L7 is NOT solved. I diagnosed the exact mechanic + timing and recorded it
(registry next:) rather than fabricate a solve. L1-L6 remain solved/reproduced (20
levels total unchanged). The transforms-during-maze extension the task asked for is
moot -- L7 doesn't need transforms.
