     solver: "PROGRAM-EDITOR mechanic (FULLY RE'd 2026-06-17). The object runs an N-slot MOVE-PROGRAM (vkuvtkaerv); each slot holds a command code (tn36.py:2171 okllwtboml: 0=settle,1=left,2=right,3=down,33=up,5/6/7/16=rotate,8/9=scale+/-,14/15/63=property). Step CSPOIQWER=4. TOOL PALETTE = a 6-BIT code editor per slot: bit b's toggle-button is at (slot_x, slot_y_top + 3*b) for b=0..5 (values 1,2,4,8,16,32), so ANY code = sum of its set bits (down 3=bit0+bit1; up 33=bit0+bit5; scale+ 8=bit3; rotate+90 5=bit0+bit2). Slot positions ARE READABLE (controller.pfyayhyovw[i].{x,y}) and RE-LAY-OUT per level (L1: 5 slots; L2: 4 slots; different x/y) -> DISCOVER, don't hardcode. RUN by clicking the object sub-button sxhtkytekm (center, discovered). L1: program [3,3,3,3,3]=5 downs->y13->33. L2: [33,33,33,33]=4 ups->y24->8."
     reproduce: "scripts/arc3_tn36_offline_solver.py — GENERAL from-scratch solver: reads obj/target deltas + the per-level button layout (pfyayhyovw), computes the move-program (down/up/left/right + scale/rotate), edits slots via bit-toggle clicks, runs, and CHAINS levels. Reproduces L1-L3 (reproduced=True claimed_level=3, 25 clicks). PATH-ROUTING: some levels have wall OBSTACLES (bizgpiltwm) with a gap; cwtesiybfx (tn36.py:2269) reverts a move that collides, so the move ORDER must route the object through the gap. The solver computes the move MULTISET from deltas then searches orderings (the game is the path oracle) until one wins -> two-pass (discover winning order per level, then clean minimal replay on a fresh env, since env.reset() does NOT rewind an advanced episode). L3: gap at y[16,20) between walls at x45; winning order [33,2,2,2,33,2]. L4: SCALE<->collision interaction -- the object box changes size when scaled, so the SCALE-down move must be interleaved at the right point (straight [3,3,3,3,1,9] LOSES; winner e.g. [3,9,3,1,3,3]); the ordering search finds it. GOTCHA: a FRESH env is required per ordering attempt -- accumulating failed runs on one env trips the game's LOSS condition and resets the whole episode to L0 (was masking L4). L5: rotation (270->0=code5) + scale-up (code8) + PROPERTY change (sjmtdfxdrc 11->15 = code 63). PROPERTY codes DECODED 2026-06-17 (set sjmtdfxdrc absolutely): code14->9, code15->8, code63->15 (PROP_CODE map; code 63 = all 6 bits set). L6: MULTI-RUN MAZE -- the collision-free path (8 moves) exceeds the 6 slots, so it uses the CHECKPOINT mechanic (wgzwawbgew): a run that ENDS on a checkpoint advances the object's base (mnvoffrbex), so progress carries across runs. Solver reads box/obstacles/checkpoints from internal state, BFS-plans a path start->checkpoint->target with each leg <= n moves, runs the legs in sequence. L6: leg1 [2,2,2,2,33,33]->checkpoint(49,20), leg2 [1,1,33,33,33,1]->target. Reproduces L1-L6 (reproduced=True claimed_level=6, 74 clicks). Frozen trajectory at results/arc_explore_trajectory_tn36.json."
